Unless I am missing something, `prepared` is built asynchronously. Consequently, we don't really need the complex `index` logic, and we can use the builder index function.


```suggestion
		const worker = async (index: number): Promise<void> => {
			if (index >= prepared.length) {
				return;
			}
			results[index] = await this.executePreparedTool(prepared[index]);
		};

		await Promise.all(
			Array.from({ length: Math.min(limit, prepared.length) }, (_, k) =>
				worker(k),
			),
		);
```

